\
Evaluate the Mathematics Notebooks by following the steps:\
\
1. Download all files above to a folder on your machine.\
2. Open \'93ProofCode1-6CapGenerator.nb\'94 and evaluate the command, \'93SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];\'94 (It is the first command.)  This will set the Mathematica directory to the folder you created.\
3. Evaluate the cells in the following notebooks in the order they appear: \
	a) ProofCode1-6CapGenerator.nb		First Notebook\
	b) ProofCode2-ColoredCapsOnReducer.nb	Second Notebook\
	c) ProofCode3-ColoringTable.nb			Third Notebook.\
4. Or, evaluate the cells in \'93ProofCode3-ColoringTable.nb\'94 directly (see why below).\
\
The meaning of the files is as follows:\
\
1. ProofCode1-6CapGenerator.nb is the first Mathematica notebook and generates the file, \'93PlanarSixCaps.mx.\'94  PlanarSixCaps.mx is a binary datafile that can be imported using the command:\
\
PCaps = Import[\'93PlanarSixCaps.mx\'94];\
\
2. \'93ProofCode2-ColoredCapsOnReducer.nb\'94 is the second Mathematica notebook that imports \'93PlanarSixCaps.mx\'94 and generates \'93ReducerColoredCaps.mx.\'94 This file is also a compressed binary version of an array that can be manipulated (after importing) in Mathematica.\
\
3. \'93ProofCode3-ColoringTable.nb\'94 is the third Mathematica notebook. It imports both \'93ReducerColoredCaps.mx\'94 and \'93BirkhoffResults.mx\'94 and can be used to \
\
\pard\tx720\tx1007\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	a) check the colorings of the planar caps that can be \
		colored on the reducer,\
	b) exhibit at least one 4-face coloring of a capped \
		state on the Birkhoff diamond for each such colored \
		cap,\
	c) confirm that the exhibited capped state corresponds \
		to the cap given by the reducer, and\
	d) display the data nicely formatted in a table.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
Only the third Mathematics notebook needs to be run as we have included all the \'93*.mx\'94 files for it already. The first two notebooks are there to explain how those files are generated and can be used to verify the included \'93*.mx\'94 files are the same files. The file \'93BirkhoffResults.mx\'94 was generated by another notebook and not provided. However, all the commands needed to verify Proposition 5.1 in the article are provided and explained in the third notebook.\
\
All files evaluate correctly on versions 13 and 14 of Mathematica. If you are on version 82 of Mathematica one hundred years from now, please have an AI rewrite the code for you.\
